  "findings": [
    "Four controls pass on original deduplicator/paginator with synthetic API/throttle: prototype ID singleton false duplicate, heuristic duplicate ID not added so later sameID with different metadata escapes, nulltrack rejects scan,1999ms duplicate versus2000ms retained. No Spotify or removal call.",
    "Track identity exact ID or raw name:first artist plus duration tolerance; no file bytes/audio fingerprint, no Unicode/case normalization. IDnull skipped. Colon composite key can collide, secondary artists/album/version ignored. Paginator reconstructs href offset/limit dropping existing query and schedules allpages; no snapshot consistency metadata.",
    "Removal source-only: starred reject lacks return and may continue queueing; recursive removal not awaited/returned, playlist.duplicates never refreshed, queue task errors not wired to outer reject; completion/hang behavior needs synthetic-only controls. No removal invoked. Functional duplicated list component references this.props instead of destructured callback. No ReactNative runtime qualification.",
    "Three original-body synthetic controls pass: non-ok API returnsnull and paginator turnsnull into zero successful pages; middleware getUserPlaylists({limit:50}) passes options as userId so intended limit ignored; reducer matches missing uri values across distinct playlist IDs, updating both. No network/removal/account access.",
    "Library Cancel only navigation.goBack, no AbortSignal/cancel action passed; middleware scan loop continues sequential playlists and has no explicit failure state. Removal success clears duplicate array without independently rerunning scan in reducer; underlying remove method promise behavior previously unqualified. Source-only ReactNative orchestration, no real UI run.",
    "getGeneric option serialization joins with equals and always prefixes ampersand rather than choosing question mark; no request deadline/status/retry metadata or pagination snapshot. API removal response status failure null not rejected. These are source observations; real Spotify endpoint compatibility not checked.",
    "Seven UI/session sources fully read, no native app/login execution. Login outer promise resolves only when access_token observed; cancellation/error paths do not call reject or resolve, initial URL may be null yet replace invoked; runtime lifecycle behavior unqualified. sessionReducer dereferences user on fetch success; API failure-null handling may fail there. No credentials or browser accessed.",
    "Auth selects username rather than token validity; home navigation waits login action promise but no visible expiry/session recovery state. Progress bar Math.max6 makes actual0 visually nonzero and no upper bound for values>100; ordinary selector outputs0..100 with static list. About Safe statement broader than reproduced heuristic identity guarantees; not treated as correctness proof.",
    "Ten additional files whole-read including app entry/render-only test,MIT2018JoseMPerez license and buildconfigs. Sole original tracked test renders App and asserts truthy; not executed, does not exercise track identity/pagination/removal/cancel. All seven authored controls remain separate evidence.",
    "Pinned package uses Expo25/ReactNative0.52/React16.2/JestExpo25, no lockfile in27blobtree. Runtime installation/build not attempted; historical dependency/API compatibility unqualified. Git precommit hook can format/add files if installed, no hooks/install/eject invoked. README links master GIF separately from pinned tracked GIF; will inspect pinned artifact and not assume mutable remote identity."
